cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you build on this idea or code, please cite it as below."
title: "How Many Failure Types Are Still Undiscovered? Species-Richness Estimators for Testing Machine-Learning Models"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kansal
    given-names: Parit
    website: "https://paritkansal.in"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ParitKansal/undiscovered-failures"
url: "https://github.com/ParitKansal/undiscovered-failures"
date-released: 2026-10-07
version: "0.1.0"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Code for a pilot study that asks whether species-richness estimators from ecology (Chao1, iChao1, ACE,
  jackknife) can estimate how many distinct failure types of a classical machine-learning model remain
  undiscovered after testing. Failure types are planted in standard tabular datasets so the true number is
  known, and the estimates are checked against that truth and against held-out test draws.
keywords:
  - machine learning testing
  - failure modes
  - species richness
  - Chao1
  - tabular data
